  "design": {
    "decision": "Every round becomes a question of whether to bid nil now to grow the sigil, even on a hand that is only marginal for nil, because an early made nil pays off in every later round.",
    "opponent": "Its current value is public; opponents lead low and prioritize busting the team's nils as the multiplier grows.",
    "rationale": "Run-long growth is one thing rarity buys. The rare growth seeds measured −7 to −11, probably because +mult and nil-point growth is too small, so this tests compounding ×mult growth on the most reliable Nil trigger (cc-nil-made-mult fires about 39% of rounds).",
